<!--CLI Documentation — Installation
  FQN: com.machineblocks.bml.cli.documentation.Installation-->
<clidoc:Installation xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:clidoc="com.machineblocks.bml.cli.documentation">

  <baseType>
    core:Documentation
  </baseType>
  <is>
    How MachineBlocks users install the host
  </is>
  <documentation>
    Consumer project (the usual path):

        npx @machineblocks/cli init com.example.bml
        npx machineblocks validate
        npx machineblocks compile com.example.bml.bricks.MyBrick

    init calls the universal project scaffold, then records @machineblocks/cli
    as a devDependency and adds com.machineblocks.bml.Library to the project
    library. Pass --install to run npm install after that profile is recorded
    and then generate AGENTS.md the same way blockml init does. Without
    --install, AGENTS.md is generated only when AgentInstructions already
    resolve; otherwise the next step is npm install and
    npx blockml agents-md generate. On a project that blockml init
    already created, the same command adds only the missing profile and does
    not replace existing files.

    That install brings @machineblocks/render-target, @blockml/block-render-engine,
    @machineblocks/core, and the BlockML compiler packages. init also records
    @blockml/core and @blockml/cli. A bml segment in the package FQN lets
    compile map the output package to scad.

    From this monorepo while the bin is not published:

        npm install
        npx blockml validate

    The second command checks these BML libraries. It is the toolchain CLI used
    to develop this repo, not the MachineBlocks user command.

    Requires Node.js 20 or newer.

    Domain users should not be sent to npm link of the blockml monorepo. The
    universal installation note that says "install @machineblocks/cli from the
    MachineBlocks mono-repo" now means this package (@machineblocks/cli in the
    machineblocks-renderer repository). @machineblocks/core remains the separate
    domain library.

  </documentation>
  <references>
    <see type="clidoc:Introduction" relation="SeeAlso" />
  </references>
</clidoc:Installation>
